      "settings": {
        "heading": "Bodology for PCOS:\nThe Studies",
        "subtext": "Insulin resistance sits underneath most PCOS symptoms. When cells stop responding to insulin, the body makes more of it — and high insulin pushes the ovaries toward androgen production and disrupts ovulation. That's why every study below starts with insulin. Here they are, laid out straight."
      }
